 {
  "id": "S075",
  "article_id": "gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1",
  "title": "Here's What a $25,000 Investment in Nvidia Could Be Worth if History Repeats Itself",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-03",
  "article_opening": "The artificial intelligence chip giant Nvidia ( NVDA +2.48% ) has struggled recently and is now down nearly 13% over the past month (as of July 1). After years of an incredible AI rally, doubts are now creeping into investors' minds.\nThere are questions about whether the large tech companies can continue to invest hundreds of billions annually in AI infrastructure, which is driving much of the cycle, and whether constraints such as energy and power will eventually have a real impact. For Nvidia ",
  "passage": "…models, called Compute Unified Device Architecture (CUDA) .\nNvidia launched CUDA in 2006 and has built a whole ecosystem around it, so this is easier said than done, but it nonetheless represents a substantial part of Nvidia's moat and therefore would be devastating to the company if CUDA loses its grip on the market.\nAs you can see in the chart above, Nvidia has had an average forward price-to-earnings ratio of nearly 34 for the past two years. Wall Street consensus estimates suggest the company will earn adjusted earnings per share of $8.97 in its current fiscal year.\nApplying a 34 forward P/E, the stock would be worth roughly $305 per share, implying about 54% upside from current levels. This means a $25,000 investment in Nvidia would be worth over $38,400 if history repeats itself.\nNow, investors should understand that there's no guarantee this plays out. Nvidia, at its current market cap, is up against the law of large numbers. As companies get more mature, they typically face lower multiples. Competition could also be a real concern.\nHowever, Nvidia has traded at a 34 forward P/E before, so it could do so again should the company prove investors wrong about their concerns.\nHere's What a $25,000 Investment in Nvidia Could Be Worth if History Repeats Itself\nBy Bram Berkowitz – Jul 3, 2026 at 12:05PM EST",
  "statement": "This means a $25,000 investment in Nvidia would be worth over $38,400 if history repeats itself."
 },
 {
